From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: John Merchant <john@johnmerchant.dev>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 02:40:55 +1030
Subject: [PATCH 13/42] hw/dma: Add the i.MX21 DMA controller

The i.MX21's DMAC has sixteen channels, each with its own interrupt, and
32 request lines from the peripherals. The stock Chumby kernel uses it
for audio (the TSC2100 driver chains SSI1 transfers period by period
with RPT and ACRPT, and reads CCNR for the playback position) and offers
it to user space through /dev/udma (chumby_udma.c) for memory-to-memory
copies with 2D geometry, checking the error status registers on every
interrupt.

Model the channels' linear (incrementing or decrementing), 2D and FIFO
ends with 8-, 16- and 32-bit ports, request-driven bursts (BLR bytes per
request while the request stays asserted) and free-running memory-to-
memory transfers, repeat with automatic clear, forced bursts, CCNR, the
interrupt status and mask, and the transfer error status for bus errors.
The request lines are the device's GPIO inputs. The timeouts are not
modelled and transfers take no time.

Signed-off-by: John Merchant <john@johnmerchant.dev>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01B1fN5Fc77Z6fVVe4rWJxPT
